# (build 129c) The pause through the sound driver's own pause flag
# (cfE8_MusPause), as the ROM has it. The pause sound's flag walks nine
# tracks turning each down; its test for an unused track branches into the
# unpause walk's step, so from the first unused track on -- here the first
# effect track, unused -- the rest are turned back up to their volumes, the
# special track is given back, and the flag returns without ending the pause
# track (its next byte does). Up to 129b the port skipped the unused track
# and went on turning down. On Motavia under its music the pause is silent
# either way; what differs is the sequencer's writes: 2642 both, the hash
# $F1E4E5B7 on 129b, $E34E7B33 on 129c-132a. (build 132b) $1DF0A957: the
# same 2642 writes, but SetMaxRelRate's as the ROM's -- the pause jingle's
# echo on FM5 writes $81, $86, $8B and $90 (FM4 op1's SSG-EG), no longer
# $81, $85, $89, $8D.

start slot 1 routes/saves/jet_scooter.json
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen level
wait idle
sound render on
wait ticks 60
expect sound playing         # Motavia's music
press start
wait ticks 90
shot 01_paused
expect sound silent          # the music turned down, the driver stopped
expect sound-writes 2642 $1DF0A957
